WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.602
-You were nice enough
to do our show

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.437
when we were in our other studio
with no audience.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.639
And here we are,
back in the main studio...

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.040
-Yeah.
-...with an audience.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.375
How does that feel?
-They like it.

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.077
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I mean, isn't that amazing?

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.179
Doesn't that sound great?
-Yeah.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.614
-I mean, it feels right, right?
-Yeah.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.583
I mean, it must be a -- it's --
just a sea change for you.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:20.219
-Oh, it was -- Really,
I mean, honestly, this is --

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:21.588
Right now, we have 58 people,

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.922
and they sound --
I told them earlier --

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:23.957
they sound like
Madison Square Garden.

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.392
-Yeah. Yeah. My God.
-It's great.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.727
-And, then, also,
all the Zoom guests...

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:28.928
-Yeah.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.063
-...which
you're still probably doing,

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.531
but it --
this changes everything.

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:35.101
-Yeah. And people like you,
for coming into the studio,

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.903
means a world of difference
to us,

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.571
so thank you so much again
for doing this.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.806
I appreciate it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.975
I know we ask you a lot of --
a lot of favors.

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:45.144
You're like, "Yeah, dude,
I do have another job,"

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:46.346
but we always ask you to come.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.348
How are you doing?
How's -- How's --

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.982
How's the city for you --
New York City?

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:53.086
I know you just...
-I mean, it just is --

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:54.954
I just love it so much.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.655
I see something --

00:00:56.655 --> 00:01:00.326
You know, my life right now
is pretty much the same

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.997
as it was
during the lockdown

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:06.699
during last
late spring and summer,

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:11.103
but just that I now get to be
traveling through the city

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:15.174
and walking through the city
and -- and going to work.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.478
Besides that, I really --
you know, we order out for food.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:22.615
This is the most social life
that I've had in --

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.283
you know, well,
since the last time I was here.

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:25.985
-Really?
You don't go out to restaurants?

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.987
-Don't -- No, not at all.
-Oh, really? Not even --

00:01:28.987 --> 00:01:31.991
-We've tried a couple of times,
you know, sitting and --

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.659
But, you know, I --

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:36.963
We went to one, I remember,
that was on an -- an avenue,

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:41.201
not on a street,
and I was sitting there

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.036
in this sort of plastic and...
-Yeah.

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:46.872
-...you know, wood thing.
-Yeah, they build these huts,

00:01:46.872 --> 00:01:48.374
like, in the middle
of the street, yeah.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.843
-And I was sitting there
and getting drunk on sake.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:54.914
And -- And I'd sort of
look over my shoulder,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:58.551
and there'd be, you know,
a big container truck

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:02.521
coming, you know,
about a foot past my head.

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:04.624
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.592
-I just was like not --

00:02:06.592 --> 00:02:09.762
And then, also,
with the new advent of,

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:15.468
you know, in the last year --
or about a year and a half

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:18.371
of ebikes and escooters now...
-I'm out.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.840
-Like, you walk out
of one of those sheds

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.407
where the restaurant is...
-[ Chuckling ] Sheds.

00:02:22.407 --> 00:02:24.109
-...after all the sake...

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:26.179
[ Laughter ]
-Vvvvrrm!

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:30.617
-...and there's a scooter going
by with some kid going like 40.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.419
[ Laughter ]
-They go -- It goes too fast.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:34.987
How was it like
getting here tonight?

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:37.657
-Well, I mean, you just --
we were coming down Broadway,

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.959
and I was in the car
coming down.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.661
And you -- you were asking,
like, about in -- in New York --

00:02:42.661 --> 00:02:43.996
being back in New York.
-Yeah.

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:48.100
-And...you know, you just see
something every day.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.037
I was coming, and I took a left
off of Broadway onto 50th

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.771
to come over here.
-Uh-huh.

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:57.209
-And there was a -- between --
50th between --

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:02.882
I guess it would have been
7th and 8th, Broadway and 8th,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.117
there was a club that said
"Gentlemen's Club"

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.219
up at the top.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.721
It had a big vertical, you know,
marquee.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:09.855
-Yeah.
-And it said up at the top

00:03:09.855 --> 00:03:11.090
"Gentlemen's Club,"

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.059
and then down below, it said,
"Live Models."

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.561
And then, the name of the club

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:17.096
was in huge block letters
running down,

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.865
called "Mixed Emotions."

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:21.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.035
I'm --
-That's an --

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:24.236
-What would that --
Yeah, what would that be

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.471
for the strip club?

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.705
[ Laughter ]
Mixed Emotions.

00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:27.973
-You can name your club
anything.

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:29.508
-Yeah, Mixed Emotions.
-Mixed Emotions.

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:33.212
-Yes, it's like a feeling of fun
mixed with shame and regret.

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:34.847
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.449
-What an odd --
What an odd name.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.519
What an odd name choice.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.153
-For your bachelor party.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:42.688
We were gonna go to Scores,
but we ended up taking --

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:43.890
taking him to Mixed Emotions.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:48.460
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.862
This city is the greatest.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.864
But -- But you shoot the show
here in New York.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.300
Is it -- What is it like filming
something in New York...

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.402
-It is so crazy.
-...as opposed to anywhere else

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.703
in the -- in the world?

00:03:57.703 --> 00:04:00.373
You've -- You've shot
so many films and TV shows.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:03.742
-You know, years ago, I shot
a film with Robert Mitchum

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:05.577
at the Utah State Penitentiary,

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:08.982
which is
a maximum-security prison,

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.016
but it also --
it's a huge complex --

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:13.986
but it also has
a minimum-security section.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:19.459
And, you know, we go in and --
and have to go through the --

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.394
you know,
a battery of sort of security

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:23.463
and so on and so forth --

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.398
this is
many, many, many years ago.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:28.834
And then we also had
different convicts

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:33.138
that were extras in the scenes.

00:04:33.138 --> 00:04:35.307
And then
we'd all have lunch together,

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:38.444
and, actually, our caterers
would cater the lunch and...

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.146
-You'd eat with the convicts?

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.014
-Yeah, we'd eat
with the different convicts

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:44.717
that were --
that were extras in the scene.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.552
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:50.322
And, you know, a film or
television production company,

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:52.891
when they film on location,
it's like an invasion.

00:04:52.891 --> 00:04:56.462
I mean, they really...

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:59.732
You get a permit to shoot
where you're gonna --

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.701
you know, the block or the house
or the --

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.735
wherever it is -- the road,

00:05:03.735 --> 00:05:06.105
and you own that spot.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:09.909
I mean, you're showing up
with trucks and campers...

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.844
-Lighting.
-...and hundreds of people

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.046
and, you know,
cables everywhere.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:16.682
I mean, you own that spot.
-Yeah.

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:19.384
And shooting
at the Utah State Penitentiary

00:05:19.384 --> 00:05:23.089
was the only place that
I'd ever been filming

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.658
where there was never a second

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:28.227
where you thought
that you owned that spot

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.897
or that you were in charge
in any way.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:33.232
-No. You're in a prison.
-Yeah. You're in a -- Yeah.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.566
And -- And you're --

00:05:34.566 --> 00:05:36.702
And it wasn't even really
the administrators

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:39.038
that felt like
they were in charge.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.339
I mean, obviously, they're --
you know,

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:44.744
it felt like the convicts
are in charge of that territory.

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:46.912
You know, they're --
they're seated a certain --

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:49.581
you know, that space,
and that's -- they're in charge.

00:05:49.581 --> 00:05:51.451
-Oh, yeah.
-And it really felt like that.

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:54.386
It really felt like
we were guests.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:56.622
Every moment we were there,
we were guests.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.324
-And do you talk --
-That's what it's like

00:05:58.324 --> 00:05:59.926
shooting on location
in New York.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:01.694
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.495
Exactly, actually.

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:05.898
I mean, the city
is very accommodating, you know?

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.934
They give us, you know,
tax breaks and everything else.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:10.335
-Yeah, well,
you're great for the city.

00:06:10.335 --> 00:06:15.274
-Yes, but New Yorkers --
it's a fantastic --

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.642
it's so healthy --

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:20.213
New Yorkers don't ever let you
think for a moment

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:23.615
that you're in charge -- ever.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.615 --> 00:06:24.817
You know, like...
-Yeah, they don't --

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:27.186
Yeah. You're --
"Yeah, yeah, get out of the way.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:28.453
This is my bus --

00:06:28.453 --> 00:06:29.555
This is my bus stop."
-Yeah, this is -- Yeah.

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:30.789
-"Yeah, but we're filming
a scene here."

00:06:30.789 --> 00:06:31.957
They're like, "I don't care."
-"Yeah, well,

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:33.392
I'm going right over there,
okay?"

00:06:33.392 --> 00:06:34.560
-"I'm going over" -- Yeah.
-"I'm going over there, right?"

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.660
-"I'm drinking my coffee."

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.029
-So you stop filming,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.964
and you let the person
go over there, you know?

00:06:38.964 --> 00:06:40.632
-I love this city so much.
-Yeah.

00:06:40.632 --> 00:06:41.801
-Do not change. Do --

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:43.068
Never -- Never change,
New York, please.

00:06:43.068 --> 00:06:45.037
-It's the greatest,
greatest city.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:47.940
I mean, just the mix
of idiosyncrasies

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.442
just come together.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:51.076
I find -- Driving down here,

00:06:51.076 --> 00:06:52.845
I was looking at all the people
in the street,

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:57.016
and -- and it's New Yorkers
that make New York so wonderful.

00:06:57.016 --> 00:07:00.586
And -- And you realize that,
as a group, I adore them.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:03.055
You know, they're -- they're
insufferable individually,

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:05.891
but, as a group,
they're fantastic, you know?

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:07.960
'Cause you mix
all those idiosyncrasies

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.530
and eccentricities together,
and it makes this amazing stew,

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.532
you know?
-Yeah.

